WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:11.800
Compare five routes by audience, connection and where the key stays.

2
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:46.080
Staff reach the assistant through InsightsIQ, iMBrace's staff chat.

3
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:52.320
The staff chat returns a cited policy answer.

4
00:00:52.640 --> 00:01:20.400
Visitors can reach the same assistant through its hosted chat link.

5
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.920
Hosted chat returns the same cited policy facts.

6
00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:55.720
The fictional partner portal frames the hosted chat page.

7
00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:02.840
The embedded hosted page opens inside the partner portal.

8
00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:18.720
A sample server connects the portal to the assistant.

9
00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:26.400
The server-backed portal returns the cited policy answer.

10
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:34.500
Compare the cited facts returned across the demo routes.

11
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.300
The recording opens the prototype portal route.

12
00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:53.860
The fictional portal sends a question to a FlowOps workflow webhook.

13
00:02:53.860 --> 00:03:16.100
The portal shows the answer beside its request details.

14
00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:46.020
Open the workflow record behind that portal request.

15
00:03:46.020 --> 00:04:01.140
The workflow shows the question passing through its steps.

16
00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:14.020
The sample portal server keeps the assistant key away from the browser.

17
00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:31.460
The order lookup asks for the matching email.

18
00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:53.260
The matching email returns the fictional order status.

19
00:04:53.260 --> 00:05:21.540
Open the workflow record behind the order lookup.

20
00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:31.300
The skill matches the order number and email.
